/**
 * The classes the shared components draw with, for the project's UI system.
 *
 * The components — DataTable, Pagination, ConfirmDialog, Field, Omnibox, HelpPanel — ask for a
 * part by name (`ui('btn.sm')`, `ui('card')`) rather than writing one CSS framework's classes, the
 * way `Html\Form\FieldStyles` does on the server. So a section inside a Bootstrap page draws
 * Bootstrap's buttons, one inside a plain-css page the plain stylesheet's, and a project that runs
 * `project:switch-ui` keeps working: the system is read when the page runs, from
 * `window.__PRAMNOS__.ui` — which the SPA shell and `Controller::spaSection()` take from
 * `scaffold_theme` in app/app.php — not fixed when the bundle was built.
 *
 * Where a system has no class for a part — a layout utility plain CSS does not have, a modal
 * that is not Bootstrap's own script-driven one — it is a `pf-ui-*` hook, which the scaffolded
 * stylesheets of those systems style.
 *
 * Add a part by adding it to all three maps; `ui()` falls back to the tailwind map, and the
 * framework's tests check that every part exists in each.
 */

/** @type {Record<string, Record<string, string>>} */
